            0.107,
            0.885,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What is the probability of drawing a red ball and then a blue ball?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.154,
            0.749,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What is the probability of drawing 2 blue balls?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.185,
            0.886,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*11. I throw a pair of 6-sided dice. Write down an event that has a probability of 0 and an outcome that has a probability of 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.234,
            0.886,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*12. Write the sample space and calculate the probability based on the given information."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.28,
            0.885,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Two dice are rolled. What is the probability that the sum is a prime number greater than 5?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.328,
            0.886,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) A bag contains 4 red, 3 green, and 2 blue balls. Two balls are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are of different colours?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.396,
            0.886,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Three coins are tossed. What is the probability that the first coin shows heads and exactly two heads occur in total?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.443,
            0.886,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) A four-digit number is formed using the digits 1, 2, 3, and 4 with no repetition. What is the probability that the number is even?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.511,
            0.886,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) A student takes a multiple-choice test with 3 questions, each having 4 options (A, B, C, D), with only one correct answer. What is the probability that the student guesses and gets exactly 2 answers correct?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.602,
            0.885,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*13. A box contains 4 balls numbered 1 to 4. Record a sample space using a tree diagram for the following experiments:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.649,
            0.885,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) A ball is drawn, and the number is recorded. Then the ball is returned, and a second ball is drawn and recorded."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.696,
            0.886,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) A ball is drawn and recorded. Without replacing the first ball, the experimenter draws and records a second ball."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.744,
            0.742,
            0.766
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) What are the sizes of these two sample spaces?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.774,
            0.886,
            0.834
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*14. List the elements of a sample space for the simultaneous tossing of a coin and drawing of a card from a set of 6 cards numbered 1 through 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
